<p>First original album, recorded at <strong>Estúdio Asas</strong> in São Paulo and produced by <strong>Edson X</strong>. Marcelo Nicchio contributed to the concept and songwriting and recorded drums.</p><p>The album featured guest appearances by <strong>Paulão de Carvalho</strong> (Velhas Virgens), vocals; <strong>Finho</strong> (band 365), vocals; and <strong>Grupo Emosamba</strong> on the introductory vignette. Several videos from the recording sessions have been preserved.</p><p>The work was independently released on CD in <strong>1998</strong>.</p><figure class="thread-media thread-media--linked"><a aria-label="Open the Meu Querido Diário recording-session image from Estúdio Asas at full size" href="/assets/archive/music/coitado-do-proximo/1997-1998-meu-querido-diario/coitadodoproximo_00_estudioasas1997_300kb.jpg" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><img alt="Record of the Meu Querido Diário recording sessions at Estúdio Asas in 1997." decoding="async" loading="lazy" src="/assets/archive/music/coitado-do-proximo/1997-1998-meu-querido-diario/coitadodoproximo_00_estudioasas1997_300kb.jpg" width="1448" height="1086"/></a><figcaption><strong>Meu Querido Diário · Estúdio Asas · 1997.</strong><span class="thread-media-note">Record of the recording sessions for Coitado do Próximo’s first album at Estúdio Asas in São Paulo.</span><a class="thread-media-open" href="/assets/archive/music/coitado-do-proximo/1997-1998-meu-querido-diario/coitadodoproximo_00_estudioasas1997_300kb.jpg" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Open image at full size ↗</a></figcaption></figure><div class="video-library" aria-label="Videos and media" aria-labelledby="music-album-1997-video-title"><div class="video-library__head"><strong id="music-album-1997-video-title">Videos &amp; Media · 1</strong><span>Estúdio Asas · 1997</span></div><div class="video-library__group"><div class="video-library__label"><strong>Recording Meu Querido Diário</strong></div><p class="video-library__descript